<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:zeebe="http://camunda.org/schema/zeebe/1.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" id="Definitions_FraudAlertTriageAgent" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn" exporter="Camunda Modeler" exporterVersion="5.46.1" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Cloud" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="8.10.0">
  <bpmn:message id="Message_CustomerConfirmedFraud" name="fraud-confirmed">
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <zeebe:subscription correlationKey="=alertId" />
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
  </bpmn:message>
  <bpmn:process id="fraud-alert-triage-agent" name="Fraud Alert Triage Agent (Event-Driven Agent)" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:startEvent id="StartEvent_FraudAlertWebhook" name="Fraud alert received" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.camunda.connectors.webhook.WebhookConnector.v1" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="14" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
      <bpmn:documentation>Fires whenever the (fictional) real-time transaction-monitoring system posts a new fraud alert to this webhook. No polling, no scheduled job checking for new alerts - the process only exists once an event arrives. Trigger it yourself with:

curl -X POST "&lt;your webhook URL from the Webhooks tab&gt;" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "{\"alertId\":\"ALERT-6601\",\"customerId\":\"CUST-40100\",\"cardLast4\":\"2210\",\"transactionAmount\":145.50,\"transactionCurrency\":\"USD\",\"merchantName\":\"Riverside Coffee Roasters\",\"merchantCountry\":\"United States\",\"riskScore\":38,\"alertReason\":\"New merchant category for this customer, amount is modest relative to typical spend.\"}"</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:properties>
          <zeebe:property name="inbound.type" value="io.camunda:webhook:1" />
          <zeebe:property name="inbound.method" value="post" />
          <zeebe:property name="inbound.context" value="fraud-alert-received" />
          <zeebe:property name="inbound.shouldValidateHmac" value="disabled" />
          <zeebe:property name="inbound.auth.type" value="NONE" />
          <zeebe:property name="consumeUnmatchedEvents" value="true" />
          <zeebe:property name="synchronousResponse" value="false" />
          <zeebe:property name="deduplicationModeManualFlag" value="false" />
          <zeebe:property name="deduplicationMode" value="AUTO" />
          <zeebe:property name="resultExpression" value="=request.body" />
        </zeebe:properties>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_ToAgent</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_ToAgent" sourceRef="StartEvent_FraudAlertWebhook" targetRef="FraudInvestigationAgent" />
    <bpmn:adHocSubProcess id="FraudInvestigationAgent" name="Fraud Investigation Agent" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.camunda.connectors.agenticai.aiagent.jobworker.v1" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="10" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
      <bpmn:documentation>Investigates the alert (transaction cross-reference, currency conversion) and decides whether it can be cleared automatically or needs a human fraud analyst. It can be interrupted at any moment - mid tool call or not - by a "customer confirmed fraud" event arriving from outside; when that happens, everything the agent was doing is abandoned and the case goes straight to card-freeze and human handoff.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:adHoc outputCollection="toolCallResults" outputElement="={&#10;  id: toolCall._meta.id,&#10;  name: toolCall._meta.name,&#10;  content: toolCallResult&#10;}" />
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda.agenticai:aiagent-job-worker:1" retries="3" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="openaiCompatible" target="provider.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.CAMUNDA_PROVIDED_LLM_API_ENDPOINT}}" target="provider.openaiCompatible.endpoint" />
          <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.CAMUNDA_PROVIDED_LLM_API_KEY}}" target="provider.openaiCompatible.authentication.apiKey" />
          <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.CAMUNDA_PROVIDED_LLM_DEFAULT_MODEL}}" target="provider.openaiCompatible.model.model" />
          <zeebe:input source="=&#34;You are a demo fraud-investigation assistant. A real-time transaction-monitoring system has already scored this alert and handed it to you to investigate before it either closes automatically or reaches a human fraud analyst.&#10;&#10;You must invoke tools using the actual tool-calling mechanism available to you - never describe or simulate a tool call in your plain-text response, and never invent, guess, or fabricate what a tool would return.&#10;&#10;Investigation steps, in order:&#10;1. Always call CrossReferenceTransactionHistory first, with the customer ID and the card&#39;s last 4 digits. This is the same full-account, all-linked-cards history lookup the real fraud platform runs on every alert - it genuinely takes several seconds, and that is expected, not an error.&#10;2. If the transaction currency is not already USD, call ConvertToBaseCurrency to get the USD-equivalent amount before you reason about the amount. Never estimate a conversion yourself.&#10;3. Decide the outcome using this policy, evaluated in order:&#10;   - If relatedAlerts90d is 0, the alert&#39;s own riskScore is below 50, and the transaction amount in USD is under 2000: the outcome is &#39;clear&#39;.&#10;   - Otherwise: the outcome is &#39;hold-for-review&#39;.&#10;4. Call RecordInvestigationOutcome exactly once, as your last tool call, with the outcome and a short summary of your reasoning that mentions the riskScore, relatedAlerts90d, and the USD amount you used.&#10;&#10;A customer-confirmed-fraud report can arrive from outside at any moment while you are still investigating. If that happens you will simply be stopped and will not see this conversation again - there is nothing special for you to do about it, so just keep investigating normally until you reach a conclusion.&#34;" target="data.systemPrompt.prompt" />
          <zeebe:input source="=&#34;Fraud alert under investigation:&#10;Alert ID: &#34; + alertId + &#34;&#10;Customer ID: &#34; + customerId + &#34;&#10;Card ending: &#34; + cardLast4 + &#34;&#10;Transaction amount: &#34; + string(transactionAmount) + &#34; &#34; + transactionCurrency + &#34;&#10;Merchant: &#34; + merchantName + &#34; (&#34; + merchantCountry + &#34;)&#10;Monitoring system risk score: &#34; + string(riskScore) + &#34;&#10;Alert reason: &#34; + alertReason + &#34;&#10;&#10;Investigate this alert and record your outcome.&#34;" target="data.userPrompt.prompt" />
          <zeebe:input target="agentContext" />
          <zeebe:input source="in-process" target="data.memory.storage.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="=20" target="data.memory.contextWindowSize" />
          <zeebe:input source="=10" target="data.limits.maxModelCalls" />
          <zeebe:input source="WAIT_FOR_TOOL_CALL_RESULTS" target="data.events.behavior" />
          <zeebe:input source="text" target="data.response.format.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="=false" target="data.response.format.parseJson" />
          <zeebe:input source="=false" target="data.response.includeAssistantMessage" />
          <zeebe:input source="=false" target="data.response.includeAgentContext" />
          <zeebe:input target="agent" />
          <zeebe:output source="=agent" target="agent" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
        <zeebe:taskHeaders>
          <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateVersion" value="10" />
          <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateId" value="io.camunda.connectors.agenticai.aiagent.jobworker.v1" />
          <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT30S" />
        </zeebe:taskHeaders>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_ToAgent</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_ToOutcomeGateway</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="CrossReferenceTransactionHistory" name="Cross-reference transaction history" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.camunda.connectors.HttpJson.v2" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="13" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
        <bpmn:documentation>Simulates the fraud platform's full-history cross-reference: a real HTTP round trip against httpbin.io's /delay/8 endpoint (a public request-echo service) standing in for a slow enterprise lookup across every account and card linked to the customer. It deliberately takes about 8 seconds - that is the window in which you can fire the second ("fraud-confirmed") webhook and watch the agent get interrupted mid-investigation. The related-alert count itself is computed deterministically from the customer ID so the demo is reproducible.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda:http-json:1" retries="2" />
          <zeebe:ioMapping>
            <zeebe:input source="=false" target="ignoreNullValues" />
            <zeebe:input source="noAuth" target="authentication.type" />
            <zeebe:input source="GET" target="method" />
            <zeebe:input source="https://httpbin.io/delay/8" target="url" />
            <zeebe:input source="={&#10;  customerId: fromAi(toolCall.customerId, &#34;The customer ID whose transaction history should be cross-referenced.&#34;, &#34;string&#34;),&#10;  cardLast4: fromAi(toolCall.cardLast4, &#34;The last 4 digits of the card used in the alerted transaction.&#34;, &#34;string&#34;)&#10;}" target="queryParameters" />
            <zeebe:input source="=false" target="storeResponse" />
            <zeebe:input source="=15" target="connectionTimeoutInSeconds" />
            <zeebe:input source="=15" target="readTimeoutInSeconds" />
          </zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:taskHeaders>
            <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateVersion" value="13" />
            <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateId" value="io.camunda.connectors.HttpJson.v2" />
            <zeebe:header key="resultExpression" value="={&#10;  relatedAlerts90d: modulo(number(substring(customerId,6)), 4),&#10;  toolCallResult: &#34;Cross-referenced &#34; + customerId + &#34; (card ending &#34; + cardLast4 + &#34;) across all linked accounts and cards: &#34; + string(modulo(number(substring(customerId,6)), 4)) + &#34; related fraud alert(s) in the last 90 days.&#34;&#10;}" />
            <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT5S" />
          </zeebe:taskHeaders>
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="ConvertToBaseCurrency" name="Convert to base currency" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.camunda.connectors.HttpJson.v2" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="13" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
        <bpmn:documentation>Converts a non-USD transaction amount to USD via the free, public frankfurter.app exchange-rate API (European Central Bank reference rates, no key required), so the agent's USD-amount policy check is comparing like with like.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda:http-json:1" retries="2" />
          <zeebe:ioMapping>
            <zeebe:input source="=false" target="ignoreNullValues" />
            <zeebe:input source="noAuth" target="authentication.type" />
            <zeebe:input source="GET" target="method" />
            <zeebe:input source="https://api.frankfurter.app/latest" target="url" />
            <zeebe:input source="={&#10;  amount: fromAi(toolCall.amount, &#34;The transaction amount in its original currency, to convert to USD.&#34;, &#34;number&#34;),&#10;  from: fromAi(toolCall.fromCurrency, &#34;The transaction&#39;s original currency code, e.g. NOK or EUR.&#34;, &#34;string&#34;),&#10;  to: &#34;USD&#34;&#10;}" target="queryParameters" />
            <zeebe:input source="=false" target="storeResponse" />
            <zeebe:input source="=20" target="connectionTimeoutInSeconds" />
            <zeebe:input source="=20" target="readTimeoutInSeconds" />
          </zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:taskHeaders>
            <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateVersion" value="13" />
            <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateId" value="io.camunda.connectors.HttpJson.v2" />
            <zeebe:header key="resultExpression" value="={&#10;  convertedAmountUSD: response.body.rates.USD,&#10;  toolCallResult: &#34;Converted &#34; + string(response.body.amount) + &#34; &#34; + response.body.base + &#34; to &#34; + string(response.body.rates.USD) + &#34; USD (ECB reference rate).&#34;&#10;}" />
            <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT5S" />
          </zeebe:taskHeaders>
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:scriptTask id="RecordInvestigationOutcome" name="Record investigation outcome">
        <bpmn:documentation>Call this exactly once, as your last action, to report the investigation outcome and your reasoning.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:script expression="=investigationOutcome" resultVariable="investigationOutcome" />
          <zeebe:ioMapping>
            <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(toolCall.investigationOutcome, &#34;The outcome: &#39;clear&#39; to close the alert automatically, &#39;hold-for-review&#39; to send it to a human fraud analyst.&#34;, &#34;string&#34;)" target="investigationOutcome" />
            <zeebe:input source="=fromAi(toolCall.investigationSummary, &#34;A short summary of your reasoning, mentioning the riskScore, relatedAlerts90d, and the USD amount you used.&#34;, &#34;string&#34;)" target="investigationSummary" />
            <zeebe:output source="=investigationOutcome" target="investigationOutcome" />
            <zeebe:output source="=investigationSummary" target="investigationSummary" />
            <zeebe:output source="=investigationOutcome + &#34;: &#34; + investigationSummary" target="toolCallResult" />
          </zeebe:ioMapping>
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
      </bpmn:scriptTask>
    </bpmn:adHocSubProcess>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="Boundary_CustomerConfirmedFraud" name="Customer confirmed fraud" attachedToRef="FraudInvestigationAgent" cancelActivity="true" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.camunda.connectors.webhook.WebhookConnectorBoundary.v1" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="14" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
      <bpmn:documentation>A second, independent webhook. If the (fictional) fraud platform's phone/chat channel confirms with the customer that the transaction is fraudulent - at any point while the agent is still investigating, whether it is mid tool-call or about to conclude - this interrupts the ad-hoc subprocess immediately and unconditionally. There is no gateway, no confidence threshold, and no prompt instruction involved: the BPMN structure itself guarantees that a confirmed-fraud event always wins over whatever the agent was reasoning about.

Trigger it yourself, correlated by alertId, with:

curl -X POST "&lt;your webhook URL from the Webhooks tab&gt;" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "{\"alertId\":\"ALERT-6601\",\"confirmedBy\":\"customer-callback\",\"confirmationNotes\":\"Customer states they did not make this purchase and have no knowledge of the merchant.\",\"confirmedAt\":\"2026-07-29T10:15:00Z\"}"</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:properties>
          <zeebe:property name="inbound.type" value="io.camunda:webhook:1" />
          <zeebe:property name="inbound.method" value="post" />
          <zeebe:property name="inbound.context" value="fraud-confirmed" />
          <zeebe:property name="inbound.shouldValidateHmac" value="disabled" />
          <zeebe:property name="inbound.auth.type" value="NONE" />
          <zeebe:property name="consumeUnmatchedEvents" value="true" />
          <zeebe:property name="synchronousResponse" value="false" />
          <zeebe:property name="correlationKeyExpression" value="=request.body.alertId" />
          <zeebe:property name="deduplicationModeManualFlag" value="false" />
          <zeebe:property name="deduplicationMode" value="AUTO" />
          <zeebe:property name="resultExpression" value="={&#10;  confirmedBy: request.body.confirmedBy,&#10;  confirmationNotes: request.body.confirmationNotes,&#10;  confirmedAt: request.body.confirmedAt&#10;}" />
        </zeebe:properties>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_InterruptToPrepare</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:messageEventDefinition id="MsgDef_CustomerConfirmedFraud" messageRef="Message_CustomerConfirmedFraud" />
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_ToOutcomeGateway" sourceRef="FraudInvestigationAgent" targetRef="Gateway_InvestigationOutcome" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_InvestigationOutcome" name="Investigation outcome?" default="Flow_HoldForReview">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_ToOutcomeGateway</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Clear</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_HoldForReview</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Clear" name="clear" sourceRef="Gateway_InvestigationOutcome" targetRef="CloseAlertNotification">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=investigationOutcome = "clear"</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_HoldForReview" name="hold for review" sourceRef="Gateway_InvestigationOutcome" targetRef="UserTask_ReviewFraudAlert" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="CloseAlertNotification" name="Close alert notification" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.camunda.connectors.HttpJson.v2" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="13" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
      <bpmn:documentation>Posts the automatic clearance to httpbin.io's echo endpoint (a stand-in for a real customer-notification/case-management system).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Clear</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_ToAlertClearedEnd</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda:http-json:1" retries="2" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="noAuth" target="authentication.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="POST" target="method" />
          <zeebe:input source="https://httpbin.io/post" target="url" />
          <zeebe:input source="=false" target="storeResponse" />
          <zeebe:input source="=false" target="followRedirects" />
          <zeebe:input source="=20" target="connectionTimeoutInSeconds" />
          <zeebe:input source="=20" target="readTimeoutInSeconds" />
          <zeebe:input source="={&#10;  alertId: alertId,&#10;  customerId: customerId,&#10;  investigationOutcome: investigationOutcome,&#10;  investigationSummary: investigationSummary&#10;}" target="body" />
          <zeebe:input source="=false" target="ignoreNullValues" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
        <zeebe:taskHeaders>
          <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateVersion" value="13" />
          <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateId" value="io.camunda.connectors.HttpJson.v2" />
          <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT5S" />
        </zeebe:taskHeaders>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_ToAlertClearedEnd" sourceRef="CloseAlertNotification" targetRef="EndEvent_AlertCleared" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_AlertCleared" name="Alert cleared automatically">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_ToAlertClearedEnd</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:userTask id="UserTask_ReviewFraudAlert" name="Review flagged fraud alert">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:userTask />
        <zeebe:formDefinition formId="fraud-alert-review" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_HoldForReview</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_ToAnalystGateway</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_ToAnalystGateway" sourceRef="UserTask_ReviewFraudAlert" targetRef="Gateway_AnalystDecision" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_AnalystDecision" name="Analyst decision?" default="Flow_Dismiss">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_ToAnalystGateway</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_ConfirmFraud</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Dismiss</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_ConfirmFraud" name="confirm fraud" sourceRef="Gateway_AnalystDecision" targetRef="Gateway_HandoffMerge">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=analystDecision = "confirm-fraud"</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Dismiss" name="dismiss" sourceRef="Gateway_AnalystDecision" targetRef="EndEvent_AlertDismissed" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_AlertDismissed" name="Alert dismissed by analyst">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Dismiss</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_HandoffMerge" name="Confirmed fraud (either path)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Plain merge, no condition: joins the two ways a case can reach the fraud team - an analyst confirming fraud after a manual review, or the interrupt event confirming fraud while the agent was still investigating.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_ConfirmFraud</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_InterruptToPrepare</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_ToPrepareHandoff</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_InterruptToPrepare" sourceRef="Boundary_CustomerConfirmedFraud" targetRef="Gateway_HandoffMerge" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_ToPrepareHandoff" sourceRef="Gateway_HandoffMerge" targetRef="PrepareHandoffSummary" />
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="PrepareHandoffSummary" name="Prepare handoff summary">
      <bpmn:documentation>Builds one consistent summary for the handoff task regardless of which path was taken to get here.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_ToPrepareHandoff</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_ToFreezeCard</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:script expression="=if confirmationNotes != null then &#34;customer-confirmed-event&#34; else &#34;analyst-review&#34;" resultVariable="handoffTrigger" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:output source="=if confirmationNotes != null then &#34;Customer confirmed fraud via callback (&#34; + confirmedBy + &#34;): &#34; + confirmationNotes else &#34;Fraud analyst confirmed fraud in manual review. Analyst notes: &#34; + (if analystNotes != null then analystNotes else &#34;(none provided)&#34;)" target="handoffReason" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_ToFreezeCard" sourceRef="PrepareHandoffSummary" targetRef="FreezeCard" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="FreezeCard" name="Freeze card" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.camunda.connectors.HttpJson.v2" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="13" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
      <bpmn:documentation>Posts the card-freeze instruction to httpbin.io's echo endpoint (a stand-in for a real card-management/processor system). Reachable only via a confirmed-fraud path - either an analyst's manual confirmation or the interrupt event - never automatically from the agent's own reasoning.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_ToFreezeCard</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_ToHandoffTask</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda:http-json:1" retries="2" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="noAuth" target="authentication.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="POST" target="method" />
          <zeebe:input source="https://httpbin.io/post" target="url" />
          <zeebe:input source="=false" target="storeResponse" />
          <zeebe:input source="=false" target="followRedirects" />
          <zeebe:input source="=20" target="connectionTimeoutInSeconds" />
          <zeebe:input source="=20" target="readTimeoutInSeconds" />
          <zeebe:input source="={&#10;  alertId: alertId,&#10;  customerId: customerId,&#10;  cardLast4: cardLast4,&#10;  handoffTrigger: handoffTrigger,&#10;  handoffReason: handoffReason&#10;}" target="body" />
          <zeebe:input source="=false" target="ignoreNullValues" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
        <zeebe:taskHeaders>
          <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateVersion" value="13" />
          <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateId" value="io.camunda.connectors.HttpJson.v2" />
          <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT5S" />
        </zeebe:taskHeaders>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_ToHandoffTask" sourceRef="FreezeCard" targetRef="UserTask_FraudTeamHandoff" />
    <bpmn:userTask id="UserTask_FraudTeamHandoff" name="Fraud team case handoff">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:userTask />
        <zeebe:formDefinition formId="fraud-team-handoff" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_ToHandoffTask</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_ToEscalatedEnd</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_ToEscalatedEnd" sourceRef="UserTask_FraudTeamHandoff" targetRef="EndEvent_Escalated" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_Escalated" name="Escalated - card frozen">
